{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"kubectl-tools","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Kubernetes Tools","description":"The everyday kubectl commands from the command palette, with a default namespace and context. Deleting and applying ask first.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:kubectlTools.menu","onCommand:kubectlTools.applyFile","onCommand:kubectlTools.deleteFile","onCommand:kubectlTools.pods","onCommand:kubectlTools.services","onCommand:kubectlTools.deployments","onCommand:kubectlTools.ingress","onCommand:kubectlTools.all","onCommand:kubectlTools.nodes","onCommand:kubectlTools.events","onCommand:kubectlTools.top","onCommand:kubectlTools.describe","onCommand:kubectlTools.logs","onCommand:kubectlTools.logsPrev","onCommand:kubectlTools.exec","onCommand:kubectlTools.restart","onCommand:kubectlTools.rolloutStatus","onCommand:kubectlTools.rollback","onCommand:kubectlTools.scale","onCommand:kubectlTools.portForward","onCommand:kubectlTools.deletePod","onCommand:kubectlTools.contexts","onCommand:kubectlTools.useContext","onCommand:kubectlTools.namespaces","onCommand:kubectlTools.setNamespace"],"permissions":["terminal"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"kubectlTools.menu","title":"Kubernetes Menu...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.applyFile","title":"Apply the Open YAML File...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.deleteFile","title":"Delete What the Open YAML File Defines...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.pods","title":"Get Pods","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.services","title":"Get Services","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.deployments","title":"Get Deployments","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.ingress","title":"Get Ingresses","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.all","title":"Get Everything in the Namespace","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.nodes","title":"Get Nodes","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.events","title":"Show Recent Events","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.top","title":"Show Pod CPU and Memory","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.describe","title":"Describe a Pod...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.logs","title":"Follow Logs of a Pod...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.logsPrev","title":"Show Logs of a Crashed Pod...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.exec","title":"Open a Shell in a Pod...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.restart","title":"Restart a Deployment...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.rolloutStatus","title":"Watch a Rollout...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.rollback","title":"Undo the Last Rollout...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.scale","title":"Scale a Deployment...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.portForward","title":"Forward a Port from a Pod...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.deletePod","title":"Delete a Pod...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.contexts","title":"List Contexts","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.useContext","title":"Switch Context...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.namespaces","title":"List Namespaces","category":"Kubernetes Tools"},{"command":"kubectlTools.setNamespace","title":"Set the Default Namespace...","category":"Kubernetes Tools"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"kubectlTools.menu","key":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+K"}],"configuration":{"title":"Kubernetes Tools","properties":{"kubectlTools.namespace":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"The namespace added to commands (-n). Empty uses your current one."},"kubectlTools.context":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"The context added to commands (--context). Empty uses your current one."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Kubernetes Tools: the everyday kubectl commands from the command palette. Each one is typed in the terminal where you can see it.\n// Deleting and applying ask first, and show the exact command.\n\nconst SAFE = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.:/@=-]{0,200}$/;\nconst safeName = (s) => (SAFE.test(String(s || '').trim()) ? String(s).trim() : null);\n\n/** `kubectl` with the namespace and context from the settings. Both are checked before they go into a command. */\nfunction base(ns, ctx) {\n  let c = 'kubectl';\n  if (ctx && safeName(ctx)) c += ' --context ' + safeName(ctx);\n  if (ns && safeName(ns)) c += ' -n ' + safeName(ns);\n  return c;\n}\n\nfunction actions(k) {\n  return [\n    { id: 'pods', title: 'Get Pods', cmd: k + ' get pods -o wide' },\n    { id: 'services', title: 'Get Services', cmd: k + ' get svc' },\n    { id: 'deployments', title: 'Get Deployments', cmd: k + ' get deploy' },\n    { id: 'ingress', title: 'Get Ingresses', cmd: k + ' get ingress' },\n    { id: 'all', title: 'Get Everything in the Namespace', cmd: k + ' get all' },\n    { id: 'nodes', title: 'Get Nodes', cmd: 'kubectl get nodes -o wide' },\n    { id: 'events', title: 'Show Recent Events', cmd: k + ' get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp' },\n    { id: 'top', title: 'Show Pod CPU and Memory', cmd: k + ' top pods' },\n    { id: 'describe', title: 'Describe a Pod...', cmd: k + ' describe pod {name}', ask: 'pod' },\n    { id: 'logs', title: 'Follow Logs of a Pod...', cmd: k + ' logs -f --tail=200 {name}', ask: 'pod' },\n    { id: 'logsPrev', title: 'Show Logs of a Crashed Pod...', cmd: k + ' logs --previous --tail=200 {name}', ask: 'pod' },\n    { id: 'exec', title: 'Open a Shell in a Pod...', cmd: k + ' exec -it {name} -- sh', ask: 'pod' },\n    { id: 'restart', title: 'Restart a Deployment...', cmd: k + ' rollout restart deployment/{name}', ask: 'deployment', confirm: 'Restart the deployment {name}?' },\n    { id: 'rolloutStatus', title: 'Watch a Rollout...', cmd: k + ' rollout status deployment/{name}', ask: 'deployment' },\n    { id: 'rollback', title: 'Undo the Last Rollout...', cmd: k + ' rollout undo deployment/{name}', ask: 'deployment', confirm: 'Roll back the deployment {name} to the previous revision?' },\n    { id: 'scale', title: 'Scale a Deployment...', cmd: k + ' scale deployment/{name} --replicas={n}', ask: 'deployment', askNumber: 'how many replicas', confirm: 'Scale {name}?' },\n    { id: 'portForward', title: 'Forward a Port from a Pod...', cmd: k + ' port-forward {name} {port}:{port}', ask: 'pod', askPort: true },\n    { id: 'deletePod', title: 'Delete a Pod...', cmd: k + ' delete pod {name}', ask: 'pod', confirm: 'Delete the pod {name}? A deployment will start a new one.' },\n    { id: 'contexts', title: 'List Contexts', cmd: 'kubectl config get-contexts' },\n    { id: 'useContext', title: 'Switch Context...', cmd: 'kubectl config use-context {name}', ask: 'context', confirm: 'Switch the kubectl context to {name}?' },\n    { id: 'namespaces', title: 'List Namespaces', cmd: 'kubectl get namespaces' },\n    { id: 'setNamespace', title: 'Set the Default Namespace...', cmd: 'kubectl config set-context --current --namespace={name}', ask: 'namespace' },\n  ];\n}\n\nfunction build(a, name, extra = {}) {\n  if (!a.ask) return a.cmd;\n  const n = safeName(name);\n  if (!n) return null;\n  let cmd = a.cmd.replace(/\\{name\\}/g, n);\n  if (a.askNumber) {\n    const r = Number(extra.n);\n    if (!Number.isInteger(r) || r < 0 || r > 1000) return null;\n    cmd = cmd.replace('{n}', String(r));\n  }\n  if (a.askPort) {\n    const p = Number(extra.port);\n    if (!Number.isInteger(p) || p < 1 || p > 65535) return null;\n    cmd = cmd.replace(/\\{port\\}/g, String(p));\n  }\n  return cmd;\n}\n\nexports._test = { base, actions, build, safeName };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const k = () => base(ferrum.settings.get('kubectlTools.namespace'), ferrum.settings.get('kubectlTools.context'));\n\n  async function run(a) {\n    let name = '';\n    const extra = {};\n    if (a.ask) {\n      name = ((await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Name of the ' + a.ask })) || '').trim();\n      if (!name) return;\n      if (a.askNumber) {\n        extra.n = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'How many ' + a.askNumber.replace('how many ', '') + '?', value: '2' });\n        if (extra.n === undefined) return;\n      }\n      if (a.askPort) {\n        extra.port = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Port number', value: '8080' });\n        if (extra.port === undefined) return;\n      }\n    }\n    const cmd = build(a, name, extra);\n    if (!cmd) return ferrum.window.showMessage('I could not make a safe command from that. Names use letters, digits and . _ - : / @ = only.', 'warn');\n    if (a.confirm && !(await ferrum.window.confirm(a.confirm.replace('{name}', name) + '\\n\\n' + cmd, 'Run it'))) return;\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n  }\n\n  for (const a of actions('kubectl')) context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register('kubectlTools.' + a.id, () => run(actions(k()).find((x) => x.id === a.id))));\n\n  /** apply or delete the YAML file that is open. */\n  async function manifest(verb) {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc || !doc.path || !/\\.ya?ml$/i.test(doc.path)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a Kubernetes YAML file first.', 'warn');\n    if (/[\"\\n\\r$`]/.test(doc.path)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The path of this file has characters I will not put in a command.', 'warn');\n    const dry = verb === 'apply' ? await ferrum.window.showQuickPick([{ label: 'Preview only (--dry-run=client)', dry: true }, { label: 'Apply for real', dry: false }], { placeholder: 'Apply ' + doc.name }) : { dry: false };\n    if (!dry) return;\n    const cmd = k() + ' ' + verb + ' -f \"' + doc.path + '\"' + (dry.dry ? ' --dry-run=client' : '');\n    if (!dry.dry && !(await ferrum.window.confirm((verb === 'delete' ? 'Delete everything in ' : 'Apply ') + doc.name + '?\\n\\n' + cmd, verb === 'delete' ? 'Delete' : 'Apply'))) return;\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n  }\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('kubectlTools.applyFile', () => manifest('apply')),\n    ferrum.commands.register('kubectlTools.deleteFile', () => manifest('delete')),\n    ferrum.commands.register('kubectlTools.menu', async () => {\n      const list = actions(k());\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(list.map((a) => ({ label: a.title, detail: a.cmd.replace('{name}', '<name>'), id: a.id })), { placeholder: 'Kubernetes' });\n      if (pick) await run(list.find((a) => a.id === pick.id));\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Kubernetes Tools\n\nGet pods, services, deployments, ingresses, nodes and events; show CPU and memory; describe a pod; follow logs (also of a crashed pod); open a shell in a pod; restart, watch or roll back a deployment; scale; port forward; delete a pod; list and switch contexts and namespaces.\n\n- **Apply the Open YAML File...** offers a **preview** (`--dry-run=client`) or the real thing, and shows the exact command before it runs. **Delete What the Open YAML File Defines...** always asks.\n- Restart, rollback, scale, delete and context switches ask first.\n- Set a namespace or a context in the settings and every command uses it.\n- Names are checked (letters, digits and `. _ - : / @ =`), so nothing you type can add a second command.\n\nAll commands are **typed in the terminal** where you see them run.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal**. It does not read output or files.\n"}}}